  [@sabamdarif](https://github.com/sabamdarif) yes, I can make the PR for that if you want or if you want, you can,
  
  [@DuilioPerez](https://github.com/DuilioPerez) did you try the command I sent above which has `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1`? also, since generally desktop environments themselves do not work in Zink+Turnip (pretty much at all) on my devices in my experience (and I believe this varies heavily by device), and only normal app windows which are not desktop environments work with Zink+Turnip, I am not confident that it would be possible to resolve the crash when hardware GPU acceleration is permitted to activate for Cinnamon itself, and even if it were, I doubt it would work even after that (XFCE exposed to Zink+Turnip is just a black screen for me, for example, though it doesn't crash)
  
  Because of that, I should explain also that it is still possible to use Zink+Turnip with individual app windows while using Cinnamon, and those other windows do not crash, it is just the Desktop Environment itself that needs `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1` to be set, so after that, you can use Zink+Turnip again by opening a terminal and typing `unset LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE`, and then running the program you want to have GPU acceleration in that window. Example:
  
  ![Image](https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/31490854/497506399-9a5013c3-66a1-42c3-bbb0-b479e3a64b05.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..vCIN6Q--MRW77_ws9yIqbMEB735zn96rad8MjuniXxQ)
  
