  | [![](https://news.ycombinator.com/y18.svg)](https://news.ycombinator.com/) | **[Hacker News](https://news.ycombinator.com/news)** [new](https://news.ycombinator.com/newest) \| [past](https://news.ycombinator.com/front) \| [comments](https://news.ycombinator.com/newcomments) \| [ask](https://news.ycombinator.com/ask) \| [show](https://news.ycombinator.com/show) \| [jobs](https://news.ycombinator.com/jobs) \| [submit](https://news.ycombinator.com/submit) | [login](https://news.ycombinator.com/login?goto=item%3Fid%3D26659740) | |
  
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  |  |  | [tifadg1](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=tifadg1) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659150) \| [context](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659150#26659740) \| [favorite](https://news.ycombinator.com/fave?id=26659740&auth=d00147cbc1de4ea218eb3120f3610417870395a7) \| on: [Pro1 X: A Linux smartphone with slideout keyboard](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659150 "Pro1 X: A Linux smartphone with slideout keyboard")<br>For english language, swipe typing coupled with autocorrect works astonishingly well. So much so that I use it regularly because of lazyness.<br>What segment does the physical keyboard appeal to? Youngins were born and raised touching the screen, so it's archaic to them. Old timers are jaded at this point to either wait for their dream phone or buy any cheap crap.<br>So who's the target for this 900 usd device? |
  |  |  |
  
  |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [blandflakes](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=blandflakes) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659862) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660067)\[–\]<br>Honestly, I find that it works astonishingly poorly. Autocorrect is often wrong, sometimes showing the right thing milliseconds before second-guessing itself into a totally wrong word, so now I'm having to backspace because for some reason typing the actual letters I want is bad user interface.<br>Agreed regarding target audience, though. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [flatline](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=flatline) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26660817) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659862) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660531)\[–\]<br>I turned off autocorrect years ago and never looked back. Sometimes I misspell a word but it’s better than typing a word slightly wrong and having a completely different word pop out. I’ll still use autocomplete sometimes to save some typing. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [anotheryou](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=anotheryou) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26660531) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659862) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660817) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660447)\[–\]<br>Apple? My swiftkey on android is sooo much better. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [SamBam](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=SamBam) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26660614) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659862) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660531) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26661147)\[–\]<br>I used Swype for a long time and loved it.<br>Then it was killed, and Android shipped its default keyboard ("gboard") with one that included swiping. I've used it ever since, not thinking about it, but it has _never_ been as good as Swype, and about 20% of my words are errors. I don't think about it much because their autocorrect suggestions are pretty good when you tap on a word, but it really is annoying. Honestly, it's insane that I keep swiping because it would be faster just to type than to swipe and correct every fifth word.<br>I have now downloaded Swiftkey. We'll see if it's any better. My first gripe is that the backspace key doesn't delete a whole word, which, when you're swiping, seems natural to me (either the whole word is right or it's not), but I'm sure there are settings and improvements I can make as I get used to it.<br>(Edit: The translate as you type feature is a perhaps-niche but killer feature for me. I often have to write to people in my poor Spanish, and always had to go back and forth between the Translate app and the app I was writing it. Doing it as I type is amazing.) | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [abawany](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=abawany) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26667518) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659862) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660614) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26661128)\[–\]<br>The one thing that made Swype awesome compared to GBoard is the configurability. On GBoard, it appears to be impossible to turn off auto space insertion after a predicted swipe whereas on Swype, one could turn that off: this allowed swiping away at long urls a word at a time. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [smichel17](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=smichel17) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26661128) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659862) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660614) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26667518) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26661147)\[–\]<br>Swype was killed? I still have and use it. It came preinstalled on my Galaxy S6. | |
