  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [IgorPartola](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=IgorPartola) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26660079) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659907) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659982) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660521) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659857)\[–\]<br>I guess someone has never been in a car crash. Or had to fix a problem on the train home after leaving work. Must be nice. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [reasonabl\_human](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=reasonabl_human) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26660203) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659907) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660079) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659857)\[–\]<br>Emergency mode on an iPhone is activated with physical buttons. If I’m on the train leaving work, I have my laptop in my bag...<br>This device is really interesting, but I agree that the product market fit is slim. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [IgorPartola](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=IgorPartola) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26661738) \| [root](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659907) \| [parent](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660203) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659857)\[–\]<br>I can tell you from several unfortunate emergency experiences that you don’t just call 911. In fact if you are the one in the accident, it’s often the case that someone else calls 911 before you find your phone. What you do is call or text your family/coworkers/significant other/etc. I mean I won’t buy a phone just for this use case, but someone who routinely works in harsh environments might.<br>As far as programming on the phone, I used to leave my computer at work and have a computer at home. On the commute I would only have my phone. If I am at the grocery store and the client calls and says their server is acting funny, I might not want to wait to SSH to it from home or run to the office.<br>I think this is all a moot point in that you are right: at this point most people don’t have the need for a physical keyboard. But at the same time, I think some small subset of people will want a physical keyboard. | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [dijit](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=dijit) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659857) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659907) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26660349)\[–\]<br>There are a cohort of people who abhor touchscreens for typing but there currently exists nothing that caters to them.<br>Everyone making phones caters to the 80% case, there are economic reasons for this (supply chain runoffs, manufacturing equipment and software) so making something for the remaining 20% cases is increasingly expensive.<br>To answer your question directly, me (a 31 year old white man technologist) and my friend (a 28 year old white man technologist)<br>¯\\\_(ツ)\_/¯ | |
  | |     |     |     |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | ![](https://news.ycombinator.com/s.gif) |  | [aceazzameen](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=aceazzameen) [on April 1, 2021](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26660349) \| [prev](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659857) \| [next](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=26659740#26659892)\[–\]<br>This targets me exactly! Well, sort of. The original Moto Droid was my first Android device, and I loved the slide out physical keyboard (paired with SwiftKey prediction and autocorrect!). It was the best of both worlds. I miss that typing experience.<br>This phone looks perfect! Up until I saw the processor. A snapdragon 662 sounds like it would be a step back in time.<br>So I guess I'm on the jaded list. My dream phone would have a landscape physical keyboard and a Samsung/Wacom pressure sensitive stylus. All with a flagship quality CPU/GPU. I could care less about multiple camera lenses. Anyways, never gonna happen. | |
